  "discussions_data": [
    {
      "id": "1a342f794f0711e150caf1bf30eeb85f2e0cea03",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1088874838,
          "type": null,
          "body": "So presumably this is guaranteed by Qt to be something that will always work, in previous, current, and future Qt releases?\n\nFrom the Qt 5.15 documentation, `filesSelected` is emitted when \"When the selection changes for local operations and the dialog is accepted\", and `accepted` is emitted \"when the dialog has been accepted either by the user or by calling accept() or done() with the QDialog::Accepted argument.\"\n\nThe 6.3 documentation appears to say the same thing.\n\nSo is there any place where they guarantee for which signals the connected method can assume that the dialog has not been deleted and for which signals it can't assume that?  (Presumably this is all single-threaded so that some other thread won't \"helpfully\" delete the `QFileDialog` instance out from under the `filesSelected` handler when `accepted` is emitted.)",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/guyharris"
          },
          "created_at": "2022-09-06T07:20:24.893Z",
          "updated_at": "2022-09-06T07:20:24.893Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 175259983,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 8038,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "5773049976eed8fd140cffcc9fce19c08db72a1c",
      "individual_note": false,
      "resolvable": true,
      "resolved": true,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1089249445,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "It does not appear so. There was a [similar bug](https://bugreports.qt.io/browse/QTBUG-90442) fixed in upstream Qt by [this commit](https://code.qt.io/cgit/qt/qtbase.git/commit/src/widgets/dialogs/qfiledialog.cpp?id=af738780d3efea14733c5a3b5540fa715cd6bca6)\n\nThat commit switched the delete command in `accept` to a `deleteLater()`, of which [Qt says:](https://doc.qt.io/qt-6/qobject.html#deleteLater)\n\n> The object will be deleted when control returns to the event loop\n\nThe crash occurs because the DeferredDelete event has been scheduled, and then at some point after `ExportDissectionDialog::dialogAccepted` calls the various `cf_` function, Qt's event loop processes the pending event and deletes the object (even though a member function of the object that was also triggered by a signal has not returned yet.)\n\nThe signals are also sent to the event loop, so it doesn't seem like there's a guarantee of the order in which the pending events on the event loop are handled, or order of which these signals are sent. There are ways to filter out events and suppress them, but we don't want the delete to never happen, we want it to happen after we're done with the object.\n\nIt's possible that reverting aspects of f67eccedd9836e6ced1f57ae9889f57a5400a3d7 and calling `exec()` instead of `show()` on the ExportDissectionDialog, causing it to spin its own event loop, would prevent this crash from occurring.\n\n@desowin has looked at this part of the code and might have some ideas.\n\nIt also could be possible to rewrite all the print functions so that they take ownership of the `print_args_t` and are responsible for deleting them, though that seems like a complicated way to handle this.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2022-09-06T11:32:22.715Z",
          "updated_at": "2022-09-06T12:10:30.466Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 175259983,
