        {
          "id": 1089313037,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "> It's possible that reverting aspects of f67eccedd9836e6ced1f57ae9889f57a5400a3d7 and calling `exec()` instead of `show()` on the ExportDissectionDialog, causing it to spin its own event loop, would prevent this crash from occurring.\n\nExtending the lifetime of object marked for deletion is not a solution in my opinion, but a pretty nasty workaround.\n\n> The crash occurs because the DeferredDelete event has been scheduled, and then at some point after `ExportDissectionDialog::dialogAccepted` calls the various `cf_` function, Qt's event loop processes the pending event and deletes the object (even though a member function of the object that was also triggered by a signal has not returned yet.)\n\nI don't quite understand the \"even though a member function of the object that was also triggered by a signal has not returned yet\". How is that even possible?\n\nEverything is supposed to execute in the main thread so there cannot be any races due to threading (if there are, then the code is obviously wrong). QObject destructor disconnects all slots so if the slot did not execute, it won't execute after the object was deleted. If there aren't any nested event loops *and* the code is calling `deleteLater()` instead of just using `delete` on the object, then everything should work just fine.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6496125,
            "username": "desowin",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Tomasz Moń",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
