        {
          "id": 1089401055,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Yes, I don't understand how it is possible, and I guess it's some sort of Qt bug, but with Qt 6.3 it is clearly processing the deferred deletion and deleting ExportDissectionDialog before `dialogAccepted()` finished, while `cf_write_json_packets()` is executing, so that `print_args_` gets deleted, and selectedFiles() ends up derefencing a null once control passes back from `cf_write_json_packets` to `dialogAccepted()`.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2022-09-06T13:05:36.743Z",
          "updated_at": "2022-09-06T13:05:36.743Z",
