        {
          "id": 1089887669,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "> Yes, I don't understand how it is possible, and I guess it's some sort of Qt bug\n\nIt is quite simple actually, and this is ideal example of *why* nested event loops are bad idea. It is not a bug in Qt, it is a problem in Wireshark.\n\nExportDissectionDialog destructor gets called due to a call to `MainApplication::processEvents();` in `update_progress_dlg()` (called by `delayed_create_progress_dlg()`). Remove the call to `MainApplication::processEvents()` and the problem is gone.\n\nUnfortunately removing the `processEvents()` call leads to functionality loss (no progress update to user). The long term goal to solve this (and possibly many similar issues) is to redesign the UI to not spin unnecessary event loops (i.e. remove all calls to `exec()` and `processEvents()`), but it is not trivial task.\n\nFor the time being, this MR seems good enough for me.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6496125,
            "username": "desowin",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Tomasz Moń",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/e423f0a8da1eede7f89748e5142d6915e4a636399964d35d888ed95ca85e2b50?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/desowin"
